WEBVTT

1
00:00:17.558 --> 00:00:21.981
didn't sound very welcoming in his 'welcome' speech," Ben whispered to Winnie.

2
00:00:22.001 --> 00:00:25.824
"Monsters make him nervous," Winnie whispered back.

3
00:00:26.736 --> 00:00:31.838
Mr. Freaky's noses were wiggling wildly as he tried to reassure Mayor Hubbletree.

4
00:00:31.858 --> 00:00:33.819
"Don't worry, Mayor.

5
00:00:34.119 --> 00:00:37.240
Miss Bungle and I will make sure that things are under control."

6
00:00:37.261 --> 00:00:39.421
"You'd better, Freaky!"

7
00:00:39.842 --> 00:00:41.242
Mayor Hubbletree snapped.

8
00:00:42.323 --> 00:00:45.164
"I went to a lot of trouble to arrange this field trip.

9
00:00:45.644 --> 00:00:49.546
A lot of people are very suspicious of monsters, you know."

10
00:00:50.546 --> 00:00:52.327
Dr. Bones looked impatient.

11
00:00:53.607 --> 00:00:54.868
"Don't worry, Mayor.

12
00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:57.321
Everything will be fine.

13
00:00:58.941 --> 00:01:02.922
I'll make sure that all the monsters are snug in their beds."

14
00:01:02.942 --> 00:01:07.724
"I have a coffin, not a bed," said a vampire.

15
00:01:07.744 --> 00:01:11.385
"I have a pyramid," Cleo said.

16
00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:13.065
Winnie giggled.

17
00:01:13.085 --> 00:01:16.386
"Do you think we should tell Dr.

18
00:01:16.466 --> 00:01:18.687
Bones that zombies never sleep?"

19
00:01:19.887 --> 00:01:20.947
"Wonderful, Dr.

20
00:01:20.987 --> 00:01:22.828
Bones!" the mayor was saying.

21
00:01:24.012 --> 00:01:27.334
"I look forward to receiving a wonderful report tomorrow.

22
00:01:28.035 --> 00:01:29.496
Now please excuse me.

23
00:01:30.036 --> 00:01:32.978
I have some very important work to do at City Hall."

24
00:01:34.559 --> 00:01:38.622
As the mayor left, the Doppel Gang made funny faces behind his back.

25
00:01:43.545 --> 00:01:44.446
that at once!"

26
00:01:45.006 --> 00:01:46.087
Mr. Freaky ordered.

27
00:01:48.488 --> 00:01:50.650
Dr. Bones turned to Al Normal.

28
00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:53.492
"You're in charge," she said.

29
00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:55.501
"I'll be in my office."

30
00:01:58.144 --> 00:02:00.225
Al Normal looked nervously at the group.

31
00:02:02.567 --> 00:02:04.749
"Okay, people, er, monsters!

32
00:02:05.169 --> 00:02:06.510
Let's go inside."

33
00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:10.474
Ben followed the other monsters into the museum.

34
00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:22.444
sure that you'll find many interesting things here," Al Normal began.

35
00:02:23.236 --> 00:02:29.420
"We have all kinds of fascinating exhibits—dinosaurs, rocks, plants.

36
00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:37.444
We also have a wonderful Old West exhibit and an Egyptian collection with valuable jewels."

37
00:02:37.464 --> 00:02:40.406
"Ooh! Dinosaurs!"

38
00:02:40.926 --> 00:02:42.147
said a lizard monster.

39
00:02:43.107 --> 00:02:44.628
Gaby pointed to a fountain.

40
00:02:44.648 --> 00:02:46.629
"What a pretty fountain."

41
00:02:46.649 --> 00:02:50.991
"It represents the oceans of the world," Mr.

42
00:02:51.031 --> 00:02:51.692
Normal said.

43
00:02:52.872 --> 00:02:55.173
"There's a map of the museum right here."

44
00:02:56.414 --> 00:02:58.654
He pointed to a big map on display.

45
00:02:59.935 --> 00:03:02.236
Beside it was a stand with printed maps.

46
00:03:03.316 --> 00:03:05.357
Al Normal looked at Miss Bungle and Mr.

47
00:03:05.397 --> 00:03:09.019
Freaky. "Should I show the students around the museum?"

48
00:03:09.499 --> 00:03:10.019
he asked.

49
00:03:10.039 --> 00:03:15.301
"I think they can explore the exhibits on their own," Miss Bungle said.

50
00:03:15.321 --> 00:03:20.203
"I don't want anyone to get lost," Al Normal murmured.

51
00:03:20.223 --> 00:03:22.044
"No problem.

52
00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:24.281
We can use the maps," Ben said.

53
00:03:24.301 --> 00:03:27.063
Al Normal still looked uneasy.

54
00:03:27.083 --> 00:03:32.686
"I'll be walking around the exhibits, watching to see if anyone needs me."

55
00:03:37.769 --> 00:03:41.771
bad he doesn't have more eyes," whispered a three-eyed monster.

56
00:03:45.933 --> 00:03:49.075
wonder where the Egyptian exhibit is," Cleo said.

57
00:03:49.095 --> 00:03:53.670
"I bet we can find it," Waldo replied, looking at his map.

58
00:03:54.511 --> 00:03:58.194
"Let's check out the Early Humans exhibit first," Gaby suggested.

59
00:03:58.214 --> 00:04:00.937
"I read that people used to live in caves."

60
00:04:02.018 --> 00:04:03.819
"Wow!" Mog said.

61
00:04:03.839 --> 00:04:07.282
"Maybe they're more like monsters than I thought."

62
00:04:08.383 --> 00:04:10.825
Ben and Winnie started exploring the museum.

63
00:04:13.848 --> 00:04:17.812
They looked at the cave people and then headed to the dinosaur exhibit.

64
00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:21.762
A few monsters were standing at a glass case.

65
00:04:26.084 --> 00:04:27.966
"Ugh!" cried a fish monster.

66
00:04:27.986 --> 00:04:30.767
"I thought they'd have real dinosaurs here.

67
00:04:31.328 --> 00:04:32.949
These are just dumb skeletons!"

68
00:04:33.849 --> 00:04:36.531
A tall skeleton glowered at the fish monster.

69
00:04:36.551 --> 00:04:40.514
"Are you calling skeletons dumb?"

70
00:04:41.474 --> 00:04:43.956
Waldo read aloud from a museum pamphlet.

71
00:04:44.968 --> 00:04:50.233
"It says here that ancient people thought that huge fossil bones belonged to giants."

72
00:04:51.373 --> 00:04:54.336
"Maybe they did belong to giants," Gaby said.

73
00:04:54.356 --> 00:05:02.302
"But now people know those bones really belonged to dinosaurs, which are long extinct," Waldo continued.

74
00:05:02.323 --> 00:05:05.005
"How do they know dinosaurs are extinct?"

75
00:05:05.465 --> 00:05:06.666
asked the fish monster.

76
00:05:06.686 --> 00:05:09.348
"Dinosaurs could still be roaming the earth."

77
00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:13.492
While the others argued about the bones, Ben walked around.

78
00:05:17.568 --> 00:05:21.130
He spotted a pair of zombies standing near the museum entrance.

79
00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:24.312
"They must be new students," Ben thought.

80
00:05:24.332 --> 00:05:26.633
"I didn't notice them on the bus."

81
00:05:28.174 --> 00:05:30.755
He decided to walk over and introduce himself.

82
00:05:32.536 --> 00:05:35.618
But he lost the zombies in the crowd before he could reach them.

83
00:05:35.638 --> 00:05:39.520
"Huh. Where did they go?"

84
00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:41.521
he said, looking around.

85
00:05:42.522 --> 00:05:46.384
Nearby, some people in hard hats came out of the construction area.

86
00:05:48.028 --> 00:05:52.530
"Excuse me, did you see two zombies go by?"

87
00:05:52.970 --> 00:05:53.751
Ben asked them.

88
00:05:53.771 --> 00:06:00.974
"Nope," said the first worker, whom Ben had seen at the director's office earlier.

89
00:06:00.994 --> 00:06:05.415
"Hey," said another worker with a frown.

90
00:06:05.435 --> 00:06:07.917
"Shouldn't you be with the other monsters?

91
00:06:08.877 --> 00:06:12.598
Dr. Bones doesn't like students wandering around the museum on their own."

92
00:06:12.618 --> 00:06:18.169
"Dr. Bones doesn't like anybody," the first worker muttered under his breath.

93
00:06:18.729 --> 00:06:20.829
Just then Ben heard a shriek.

94
00:06:20.849 --> 00:06:24.710
"That sounds like Cleo!"

95
00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:25.550
he thought.

96
00:06:26.291 --> 00:06:29.552
He thanked the workers and whirled around to see what was happening.

97
00:06:33.032 --> 00:06:35.113
He found his friends at the Egyptian exhibit.

98
00:06:35.673 --> 00:06:40.835
They were all staring into a tall glass display case, just past the Egyptian jewels.

99
00:06:43.875 --> 00:06:46.036
Cleo had her hands clapped over her mouth.

100
00:06:46.496 --> 00:06:47.958
"Cleo, what's wrong?"

101
00:06:48.318 --> 00:06:48.898
Ben asked.

102
00:06:49.719 --> 00:06:51.120
Cleo pointed at the case.

103
00:06:51.140 --> 00:06:52.942
"See that mummy?

104
00:06:53.302 --> 00:06:54.824
He's my uncle Tut!"
